📊 **Initial Scope for My Data Analytics Project**

I'm currently working on a data analytics project focused on building a complete reporting system for a B2B operations environment.

This is the **initial scope** I’m starting with — and it will evolve as I go deeper into the data and business needs:

### 🔹 Sales & Revenue Performance

* Total Revenue (Daily / Monthly / Quarterly)
* Revenue by Retailer / Area / Supplier
* Average Order Value (AOV)
* Revenue Growth (MoM, QoQ)

### 🔹 Order Management

* Total Orders Volume
* Order Status Breakdown
* Cancellation Rate
* Processing Time (Creation → Confirmation)
* Peak Ordering Times
* Repeat Order Rate

### 🔹 Delivery & Logistics

* On-Time Delivery Rate
* Average Delivery Time
* Delivery Success vs Failures
* Driver Productivity

### 🔹 Payment & Financial Health

* Collection Rate
* Outstanding Payments
* Payment Delays
* Bad Debt Rate

### 🔹 Retailer Behavior

* Active Retailers
* New vs Returning
* Churn Rate
* RFM Segmentation

### 🔹 Product & Supplier Performance

* Top Products (Volume & Revenue)
* Supplier Fill Rate
* Slow-Moving Products

### 🔹 Operational Efficiency

* Orders per Driver
* Utilization Rate
* Order-to-Delivery Cycle Time

---

💡 *This is a starting point, not a fixed scope. The goal is to refine these metrics based on real business insights and data exploration.*

Would love to hear suggestions or ideas from others working on similar problems.
